{{- /*
Replaces kubeadm's default kube-system/coredns ConfigMap with one
that maps the apiserver endpoint to the control-plane LB's private
IP. Pods inside the cluster (incl. CAPI components after clusterctl
move) resolve the endpoint through CoreDNS without any extra
Corefile imports or Deployment patches.

Only the private IP belongs in the hosts block. CoreDNS is an addon
the apiserver itself schedules, so it never answers before the
apiserver is reachable, and the Corefile ends in `loadbalance` — a
second A record for the same name would round-robin half of all
lookups onto an IP that gets disabled once the cluster is up.

The non-hosts portion mirrors kubeadm's default Corefile. When
upstream changes the default (rare, but happens on plugin
additions / removals), this template needs the same edit.
*/ -}}
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: coredns
  namespace: kube-system
data:
  Corefile: |
    .:53 {
        errors
        health {
            lameduck 5s
        }
        ready
        kubernetes cluster.local in-addr.arpa ip6.arpa {
            pods insecure
            fallthrough in-addr.arpa ip6.arpa
            ttl 30
        }
        hosts {
            {{ .ControlPlaneLBPrivateIP }} {{ .ControlPlaneEndpoint }}
            fallthrough
        }
        prometheus :9153
        forward . /etc/resolv.conf {
            max_concurrent 1000
        }
        cache 30 {
            disable success cluster.local
            disable denial cluster.local
        }
        loop
        reload
        loadbalance
    }
